{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והתנחלתם אותם לבניכם", :translit "u'netnachaltem otam liv'neichem", :gloss "and you shall bequeath them to your children"} {:he "והתנחלתם את הארץ", :translit "u'netnachaltem et ha'aretz", :gloss "and you shall take possession of the land"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verbal linkage (gezeirah shavah): the shared root י-ר-ש links inheritance of slaves to acquisition of land."}], :frame {:text "The term yerushah appears in connection with both slaves and land. Drawing on the verbal parallel, the Talmud derives that a Canaanite slave is acquired through the same modes as real property: money, deed, and possession (Kiddushin 22a–b; see also Gittin 40a).", :sources ["Kiddushin 22a" "Kiddushin 22b" "Gittin 40a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verbal linkage (gezeirah shavah): the shared root י-ר-ש links inheritance of slaves to acquisition of land.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:25:42.959521440Z", :model "glm-5.2"}